 "engine": "cf-whisper-large-v3-turbo",
 "sentences": [
  {
   "t": 4.6,
   "end": 5.36,
   "text": "Namaskar."
  },
  {
   "t": 7.54,
   "end": 11.12,
   "text": "The preceding sutras, from one to seven,"
  },
  {
   "t": 11.82,
   "end": 15.02,
   "text": "have intensified the attainment of the real nature,"
  },
  {
   "t": 15.32,
   "end": 19.56,
   "text": "Sarupalaba, in different ways of overcoming duality"
  },
  {
   "t": 19.56,
   "end": 21.42,
   "text": "and interiorization."
  },
  {
   "t": 22.06,
   "end": 26.1,
   "text": "From Sutra E, the attention is directed to an integration"
  },
  {
   "t": 26.1,
   "end": 29.48,
   "text": "of the inner with the outer, the self with the universe."
  },
  {
   "t": 30.74,
   "end": 36.36,
   "text": "In Sutra E, this finds expression in an unusual meaning of rasa"
  },
  {
   "t": 36.36,
   "end": 37.98,
   "text": "at three levels."
  },
  {
   "t": 38.98,
   "end": 41.36,
   "text": "Three levels of support, adhara,"
  },
  {
   "t": 42.02,
   "end": 44.72,
   "text": "which correspond to the phases of creation,"
  },
  {
   "t": 45.1,
   "end": 48.12,
   "text": "maintenance and reabsorption or withdrawal."
  },
  {
   "t": 49.38,
   "end": 52.92,
   "text": "Again and again, it is stressed that those processes"
  },
  {
   "t": 52.92,
   "end": 54.84,
   "text": "are not to be done by will,"
  },
  {
   "t": 54.84,
   "end": 60.26,
   "text": "but happen spontaneously by an inner inspirational impulse,"
  },
  {
   "t": 61.24,
   "end": 63.62,
   "text": "the Pratama Pratipha Ullasa,"
  },
  {
   "t": 63.96,
   "end": 68.42,
   "text": "which plays such an important role in the spirituality of Trika."
  },
  {
   "t": 68.42,
   "end": 73.42,
   "text": "And this threefold process leads the yogi or mystic"
  },
  {
   "t": 73.42,
   "end": 77.6,
   "text": "to entering the spontaneous Ka-mudra,"
  },
  {
   "t": 78.1,
   "end": 83.22,
   "text": "the mudra by which he moves in the space of consciousness,"
  },
  {
   "t": 83.66,
   "end": 86.14,
   "text": "which is identical with Kichari Mudra,"
  },
  {
   "t": 86.52,
   "end": 90.92,
   "text": "which is based on a state of supreme non-duality."
  },
  {
   "t": 92.0,
   "end": 94.26,
   "text": "At this time, not occasionally,"
  },
  {
   "t": 94.7,
   "end": 96.5,
   "text": "but uninterrupted."
  },
  {
   "t": 97.06,
   "end": 100.32,
   "text": "It corresponds to the state beyond the force,"
  },
  {
   "t": 100.54,
   "end": 102.5,
   "text": "generally called to Riyadita,"
  },
  {
   "t": 103.08,
   "end": 105.82,
   "text": "which pervades all the levels of consciousness."
  },
  {
   "t": 107.12,
   "end": 109.3,
   "text": "The yogi who has attained this stage"
  },
  {
   "t": 109.3,
   "end": 111.84,
   "text": "is actually a Jiva Mukta,"
  },
  {
   "t": 112.08,
   "end": 116.2,
   "text": "who is not only enlightened for himself or herself,"
  },
  {
   "t": 116.2,
   "end": 119.54,
   "text": "but who can enlighten the whole world."
  },
  {
   "t": 121.66,
   "end": 123.9,
   "text": "Now the commentator Anandha Shaktipada"
  },
  {
   "t": 123.9,
   "end": 127.94,
   "text": "gives the following introduction to Sutra 8."
  },
  {
   "t": 129.6,
   "end": 130.52,
   "text": "Quote,"
  },
  {
   "t": 130.92,
   "end": 134.36,
   "text": "Having described how by the gradual arising"
  },
  {
   "t": 134.36,
   "end": 136.64,
   "text": "of the four forms of speech,"
  },
  {
   "t": 136.9,
   "end": 140.54,
   "text": "the arise of the unobstructed sound of consciousness"
  },
  {
   "t": 140.54,
   "end": 143.9,
   "text": "shines everywhere and at all times."
  },
  {
   "t": 143.9,
   "end": 147.62,
   "text": "Now the supreme unsuppassable abode"
  },
  {
   "t": 147.62,
   "end": 152.52,
   "text": "experienced in the enjoyment of the three essences"
  },
  {
   "t": 152.52,
   "end": 154.18,
   "text": "is being explained."
  },
  {
   "t": 155.34,
   "end": 156.86,
   "text": "Sutra 8."
  },
  {
   "t": 158.76,
   "end": 161.84,
   "text": "Rasa Tritaya Asvadhanena"
  },
  {
   "t": 161.84,
   "end": 165.62,
   "text": "Anicca Ucjalitam Vigata Bhantam"
  },
  {
   "t": 165.62,
   "end": 166.92,
   "text": "Baram Brahma"
  },
  {
   "t": 168.34,
   "end": 171.5,
   "text": "By relishing the three essences,"
  },
  {
   "t": 171.68,
   "end": 173.46,
   "text": "the unbound supreme Brahman,"
  },
  {
   "t": 173.9,
   "end": 175.32,
   "text": "emerges spontaneously."
  },
  {
   "t": 176.64,
   "end": 177.32,
   "text": "Commentary."
  },
  {
   "t": 177.52,
   "end": 177.8,
   "text": "Quote,"
  },
  {
   "t": 179.68,
   "end": 181.46,
   "text": "Now some light will be thrown"
  },
  {
   "t": 181.46,
   "end": 183.2,
   "text": "on the three essences"
  },
  {
   "t": 183.2,
   "end": 186.26,
   "text": "as it has come from the mouth of the guru."
  },
  {
   "t": 186.68,
   "end": 188.52,
   "text": "And here he stresses that"
  },
  {
   "t": 188.52,
   "end": 190.6,
   "text": "it is an oral transmission."
  },
  {
   "t": 190.9,
   "end": 193.22,
   "text": "And probably you cannot understand it"
  },
  {
   "t": 193.22,
   "end": 196.64,
   "text": "without that direct transmission from the guru."
  },
  {
   "t": 197.8,
   "end": 201.72,
   "text": "While relishing the three spontaneous essences"
  },
  {
   "t": 201.72,
   "end": 204.22,
   "text": "which are experienced in Muladhara,"
  },
  {
   "t": 204.56,
   "end": 206.28,
   "text": "Payudhara, and Adhara,"
  },
  {
   "t": 206.86,
   "end": 208.32,
   "text": "the supreme Brahman,"
  },
  {
   "t": 208.54,
   "end": 210.84,
   "text": "whose nature is the unsurpassed,"
  },
  {
   "t": 211.02,
   "end": 212.56,
   "text": "most excellent consciousness,"
  },
  {
   "t": 213.02,
   "end": 214.42,
   "text": "without any desire,"
  },
  {
   "t": 214.92,
   "end": 217.36,
   "text": "it emerges free from bondage,"
  },
  {
   "t": 217.94,
   "end": 220.4,
   "text": "beyond the restraints of the world of samsara,"
  },
  {
   "t": 220.84,
   "end": 222.36,
   "text": "of the nature of duality."
  },
  {
   "t": 222.36,
   "end": 225.28,
   "text": "It is transcending completely"
  },
  {
   "t": 225.28,
   "end": 227.24,
   "text": "the nature of the dual Brahman,"
  },
  {
   "t": 227.58,
   "end": 229.96,
   "text": "consisting in a tranquil state"
  },
  {
   "t": 229.96,
   "end": 231.78,
   "text": "and a state of multiplicity."
  },
  {
   "t": 233.6,
   "end": 235.6,
   "text": "The supreme Brahman"
  },
  {
   "t": 235.6,
   "end": 237.8,
   "text": "unfolds perpetually"
  },
  {
   "t": 237.8,
   "end": 240.26,
   "text": "in a state that never sets."
  },
  {
   "t": 241.66,
   "end": 243.58,
   "text": "Now, this will be explained"
  },
  {
   "t": 243.58,
   "end": 244.64,
   "text": "in its secret"
  },
  {
   "t": 244.64,
   "end": 247.1,
   "text": "or mystical process,"
  },
  {
   "t": 247.32,
   "end": 248.4,
   "text": "Rahasya Kravena."
  },
  {
   "t": 250.62,
   "end": 251.22,
   "text": "Muladhara."
  },
  {
   "t": 251.62,
   "end": 253.4,
   "text": "And I have to say from the outset,"
  },
  {
   "t": 253.64,
   "end": 255.0,
   "text": "Muladhara doesn't have here"
  },
  {
   "t": 255.0,
   "end": 255.56,
   "text": "the meaning"
  },
  {
   "t": 255.56,
   "end": 257.4,
   "text": "which it has in Hatha Yoga"
  },
  {
   "t": 257.4,
   "end": 259.18,
   "text": "as one of the chakras"
  },
  {
   "t": 259.18,
   "end": 260.74,
   "text": "of the subtle body."
  },
  {
   "t": 261.06,
   "end": 262.3,
   "text": "It has a completely,"
  },
  {
   "t": 263.36,
   "end": 265.4,
   "text": "just the meaning of the words"
  },
  {
   "t": 265.4,
   "end": 267.58,
   "text": "that are not associated with yoga."
  },
  {
   "t": 269.32,
   "end": 269.92,
   "text": "Muladhara."
  },
  {
   "t": 270.26,
   "end": 271.72,
   "text": "The fundamental support"
  },
  {
   "t": 271.72,
   "end": 274.16,
   "text": "is of the nature of creation,"
  },
  {
   "t": 274.38,
   "end": 274.8,
   "text": "Srichti,"
  },
  {
   "t": 275.08,
   "end": 276.98,
   "text": "which is the flashing forth"
  },
  {
   "t": 276.98,
   "end": 279.4,
   "text": "of the first illuminative insight"
  },
  {
   "t": 279.4,
   "end": 282.14,
   "text": "as the great original sound,"
  },
  {
   "t": 282.56,
   "end": 283.2,
   "text": "Aha, Nada."
  },
  {
   "t": 284.06,
   "end": 285.66,
   "text": "Because it becomes"
  },
  {
   "t": 285.66,
   "end": 288.0,
   "text": "the supporting primordial background"
  },
  {
   "t": 288.0,
   "end": 289.76,
   "text": "of the consciousness"
  },
  {
   "t": 289.76,
   "end": 292.92,
   "text": "which is both dual and non-dual."
  },
  {
   "t": 293.76,
   "end": 294.92,
   "text": "Now, this background,"
  },
  {
   "t": 295.4,
   "end": 295.72,
   "text": "Pitti,"
  },
  {
   "t": 295.8,
   "end": 298.08,
   "text": "Pitti actually means a plain wall,"
  },
  {
